<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Crean half-yr pre-tax profit unchanged.</title>
<headline>Crean half-yr pre-tax profit unchanged.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1996-09-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1996</p>
<p>			   (million punts unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (p), fully diluted 14.0		   vs 12.7</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 6.5363		 vs 6.225</p>
<p> Pretax profit	    9.5		    vs 9.52</p>
<p> Turnover		   155.22		 vs 130.68</p>
<p>NOTE - Industrial holding company James Crean Plc said profit before tax was unchanged from 1995 but noted profits after tax and minorities was up 12 percent relative to the first half of 1995. Crean said this was a more meaningful comparison following the buyout of the minority shareholding in Inishtech this year.  </p>
<p> Operating profit	 13.60		  vs 12.07</p>
<p> Interest payable	 4.07		   vs 2.55</p>
<p> Tax charge		 2.37		   vs 2.35</p>
<p> Net taxed		  5.16		   vs 5.66</p>
<p> Attributable	     4.85		   vs 4.67</p>
<p> Pay date		   December 12</p>
<p>Div registration date  October 1  Ex-div date		September 23</p>
<p>NOTE - Crean said that group net borrowings at June 30, 1996, excluding 31.5 million punts of convertible loan stock, were 67.7 million compared with 25.3 million at end-June last year.</p>
<p>-- Dublin Newsroom +353 1 676 9779</p>
</text>
